From: Stained Glass OS <dev@stained-glass.example>
Subject: wine.inf: .txt and .log files open in Notepad

Wine registers txtfile (open and print with notepad.exe) but never maps
.txt to it, so ShellExecute of a text file -- a double click, `start
file.txt`, any program opening a log -- failed with "no application
associated". .txt, .text and .log are now text files, as on Windows, with
their content type and the Explorer "New > Text Document" entry; .inf files
open in Notepad (install stays a verb). The entries do not overwrite an
association already there, so a user's choice survives wineboot -u.

Gate: test/notepad-gate.sh.
---
diff --git a/loader/wine.inf.in b/loader/wine.inf.in
index 0a967e9..f4634ad 100644
--- a/loader/wine.inf.in
+++ b/loader/wine.inf.in
@@ -276,6 +276,13 @@ HKCR,.msi,,2,"Msi.Package"
 HKCR,.msp,,2,"Msi.Patch"
 HKCR,.pdf,,2,"pdffile"
 HKCR,.rtf,,2,"rtffile"
+HKCR,.txt,,2,"txtfile"
+HKCR,.txt,"Content Type",2,"text/plain"
+HKCR,.txt,"PerceivedType",2,"text"
+HKCR,.txt\ShellNew,"NullFile",2,""
+HKCR,.log,,2,"txtfile"
+HKCR,.log,"Content Type",2,"text/plain"
+HKCR,.text,,2,"txtfile"
 HKCR,.wri,,2,"wrifile"
 HKCR,*\shellex\ContextMenuHandlers,,16
 HKCR,chm.file,,2,"Compiled HTML Help File"
@@ -301,6 +308,7 @@ HKCR,hlpfile,,2,"Help File"
 HKCR,hlpfile\shell\open\command,,2,"""%11%\winhlp32.exe"" ""%1"""
 HKCR,htmlfile\shell\open\command,,2,"""%11%\winebrowser.exe"" ""%1"""
 HKCR,inffile,,2,"Setup Information"
+HKCR,inffile\shell\open\command,,2,"""%11%\notepad.exe"" ""%1"""
 HKCR,inffile\shell\install\command,,2,"%11%\rundll32.exe setupapi,InstallHinfSection DefaultInstall 132 %1"
 HKCR,inifile,,2,"Configuration Settings"
 HKCR,inifile\shell\open\command,,2,"""%11%\notepad.exe"" ""%1"""
